..
> So short of compiling our own terminfo entry on both systems (once we
> figure out how the /dev/console device handles colors), I thought I would
> post a quick question to see how others have handled this.

     When building NetHack for Unix, you were forced to choose between
terminfo and termcap.  If you chose terminfo, then of course you terminal's
entry needs to have the proper codes for color defined.  If so, NetHack
should be able to use them.  However, if you chose termcap, NetHack will
not support color.  This is due to the way some conditional code sequences
in NetHack's termcap.c are arranged--for Unix, termcap implies no color.
It's possible to make a minor change or two which will enable ANSI-style
color to work.  The VMS port uses termcap and supports ANSI color.

> (BTW: when I compiled 3.0(j) on the PC and ran with 'standout' set, it
> gave me reverse video only).

     You need to set _both_ the 'color' and 'standout' options for color
to work (true for all ports, I believe).

     3.1 will have better color support, including making color and
standout independent of each other.

